  "name": "prioritizing-my-inbox",
  "description": "Give the current user a personal, ranked shortlist of the PostHog Inbox reports they are most likely to care about right now. Reads their stored personal ranking first, with one `inbox-reports-list` call (`view=for_you`, `sort=personal`), and keeps its order and reasons. Uses `inbox-reports-for-me` for a fresh or focused list, and builds a ranking by hand from the activity summary and the ranking model's lifts only when no stored ranking applies or the user asks for custom weights. Use when the user says \"let's look at my inbox\", \"what's in my inbox for me?\", \"my top 10 inbox reports\", \"what should I look at today?\", or asks to re-rank, focus, or filter that list. For browsing, filtering, drilling into, or acting on a single report, use `inbox-exploration`.",
